The `last-input` write is not in the code below. The node's `with` clause grants only `Clock`, `HTTPClient<['feeds.example.com']>` and `Notifier<'digest'>`. Writing to a shared store would need `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0` (a `StateHandle<…, read-write>`), and this world cannot import an interface outside its grant. An approval described in the request does not change the grant. To add the write, the graph's declaration of `Heartbeat` has to gain a `StateHandle<'<store>', read-write>` in its `with` clause. Once that is in the declaration, the change is one extra `import` and a single `state_rw::put("last-input", &feed_url)` call, and the output stays the same.

